STEPS :- (ROLLING HASH CHUNKER)

Setup:
   W  = window size        (e.g. 4)
   B  = base               (e.g. 31)
   M  = big prime          (e.g. 1,000,000,007)
   D  = cut divisor        (e.g. 8)
   highPower = B^(W-1) % M   ← weight of the leftmost (MSB) char

① Calculate hash for 1st window in file:
      hash = 0
      for each of the first W bytes c:
          hash = (hash × B + c) % M
          add c to current chunk

② Repeat the following :- (until file ends)

   i)   If  chunk size ≥ MIN  and  hash % D == 0
        OR  chunk size ≥ MAX
        then CUT:
             • SHA-256 the current chunk
             • save it (hash, size, offset)
             • start a new empty chunk

   ii)  Subtract leftmost (MSB) char from hash:
             hash = (hash − old × highPower) % M
             (if hash < 0, add M)

   iii) Shift entire hash by 1 unit to left:
             hash = (hash × B) % M

   iv)  Add new character to the window:
             hash = (hash + new) % M
             add new to current chunk

③ When file ends:
      if current chunk is not empty → CUT it (last chunk)
